# Code hygiene

When the issue says it is a hygiene pass, apply this rule to every line in the files it names. Visible copy, layout, and link targets stay the same. Leave every other file alone.

On any other task, apply this rule only to lines you add or change. Leave the surrounding code as it is.

## Comments

- At most two lines.
- Say why the code is this way, or which constraint a later edit has to keep.
- Delete a comment that repeats the next line.
- Do not leave `TODO`, `FIXME`, or commented-out markup. Record a follow-up under Unresolved concerns in the pull request.

## File shape

Match the nearest page.

- An HTML page is ordered: doctype, head (charset, viewport, title, stylesheet), header, main, footer, then `script.js` when the page needs store links.
- A new page uses the existing class names. Do not invent a second visual system.
- A style used by one element stays next to the rule it modifies. A style used by two pages goes in `styles.css`.
- Do not add `console.log`.
